course: dictionary
lesson: 6452
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Napoleon is one of them: it can be a person's name, a cake, or an old coin. Context tells you which one is meant. «Napoleon was about average height for a Frenchman of his time.» Here it is a person, because a height belongs to a person.
explain: A capital N is a clue. Napoleon with a capital letter is a name. A napoleon with a small n is a thing: a pastry or an old coin. Read the words around it to decide which. Cream, bakery or cake point to the pastry. Gold, money or old France point to the coin.
explain: Always test your meaning. Put it in the sentence in place of the word and check that it still makes sense. «Its nose was damaged long before Napoleon's soldiers came.» Swap in a cake and it does not make sense, so it must be the man's name.
fact: Napoleon Bonaparte was a French general who made himself Emperor of France.
fact: He conquered much of Europe before he was defeated at the Battle of Waterloo.
fact: «Napoleon's empire at its height, around 1810 to 1812, controlled or dominated most of western and central Europe.»
fact: A napoleon is a layered pastry with cream filling, also called a mille-feuille or vanilla slice.
fact: A napoleon was also an old French gold coin.
exercise: «Its nose was damaged long before Napoleon's soldiers came.» What kind of word is Napoleon here? | An old gold coin | A cake with cream | *A person's name | A town in France
exercise: Aunt Ruth says, «Try a napoleon with your tea.» What is a napoleon? | *A layered pastry with cream filling | A famous general's horse | A small French village | A French gold coin from long ago
exercise: Which clue tells you that Napoleon is a name? | *The capital N, and the sentence is about a leader or a height | The cream in the middle | The word is very old | The word is in a bakery
test: «Napoleon's empire at its height controlled most of western and central Europe.» What does this tell you about Napoleon? | *He was a person who ruled a huge area | He was a cake sold in shops | He was a small village | He was a gold coin
test: Ella finds an old coin in a box, and the label says «napoleon». What does the word mean here? | A pastry with jam | A layered vanilla slice from a bakery | A French general's army | *An old French gold coin
exam: In the sentence «The bakery sells a napoleon, layered with cream», what does napoleon mean? | Napoleon Bonaparte, the French general | An old French gold coin | A battle won on land | *A layered cream pastry
